# What must not reach a build context.
#
# There was no .dockerignore, so every build copied the host's node_modules
# (572 MB) and apps/web/.next (237 MB) into the build context and then into the
# builder image. Slow, and worse: `next build` finds a populated .next from the
# host and may reuse parts of it, so an image can ship a mix of freshly
# compiled code and stale output — a class of bug that is very hard to read
# from the outside, because the source and the running code disagree.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Python
.venv
**/.venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__

# Secrets and local state. .env is gitignored; it must not be image-ignored
# only by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not needed to build or run a service.
.git
.github
.claude
docs
models
*.md
!README.md
